{
  "task": "C3-R1",
  "supersedes": "C3's statement that no official 2015 58-sector workbook exists",
  "source_discovery_defect": {
    "claim_made_by_c3": "No official 58-sector workbook exists; NESDC publishes 180 sectors for 2015.",
    "claim_status": "FALSE",
    "root_cause_primary": "Discovery was scoped to a SINGLE mechanism — sitemap -> /download/ pages -> each page's ?p=&ddl= redirect. The aggregated workbooks (x58, x26, x16) live in the WordPress MEDIA LIBRARY and are not linked from any /download/ page. The 2015 download page carries exactly ONE ddl link, the 180-sector file, so no amount of retrying that path could ever have found the 58-sector table.",
    "contributing_causes": [
      "`_DOWNLOAD_SLUG` matched only sitemap <loc> entries under /download/ whose slug contained \"i-o-table\" or \"input-output\". Media-library uploads never appear in the downloads sitemap at all.",
      "`resolve_download_url` returned every ddl link but the caller took `matching[0]` — the FIRST Excel link per page. A latent defect: not the operative cause here (only one link exists) but it would have hidden a second workbook on any page listing two.",
      "No filename-pattern search was performed for the published aggregation suffixes (x58 / x26 / x16), and the WordPress media REST API was never queried.",
      "The report then converted \"not found by my one mechanism\" into \"does not exist officially\" — an unwarranted negative claim."
    ],
    "causes_ruled_out": {
      "waf_cookie_handling": "NOT a cause. The bounded cookie-aware retry worked correctly; the 58-sector file downloads on the first attempt (waf_attempts = 1).",
      "same_url_redirect_handling": "NOT a cause; handled correctly.",
      "http_404_with_content_handling": "NOT a cause. HTML pages answering 404-with-body were parsed correctly, and restricting that leniency to HTML (never to file downloads) was and remains correct.",
      "download_candidate_ranking": "Not the operative cause — there was only one candidate to rank — but the first-match selection is fixed regardless."
    },
    "fix": [
      "query_the_official_wordpress_media_rest_api",
      "search_published_aggregation_filename_patterns",
      "retain_all_ddl_candidates_not_only_the_first",
      "validate_workbook_identity_before_accepting_a_file"
    ]
  },
